I doubt that many of you are old enough to remember when "Wallified
Mazes" were added to NetHack. (it was 3.3.0) but they've become the
norm for maze levels. So, I thought, why not also wallify the corridors
in the regular dungeon?

This patch replaces this...

 #   -----+-------
 #        #
 #        #
 #        #        -----
 #       ##        |   |
 # ------.-       #.   |
 d |......|     ###|   |
 G#.^.<...|     #  |   |
   |..^.$..######  |   |
   --------        -----

...with this:

- |  -----+-------
| |      | |
| |      | |
| |     -- |       -----
| |     |  |     --|   |
| |------.--   --- .   |
|d-|......|    |   |   |
|G..^.<...|----- --|   |
---|..^.$..      | |   |
   --------------- -----

Also, corridors can now occasionally contain objects, traps and/or
graffiti.

A consequence of this is that "secret corridor squares" are no longer
randomly generated - except on the rogue level. Personally I don't
consider it that big a loss - secret doors were always the more
troublesome of the pair.

